:"2026-07-05T07:21:06Z","updated_at":"2026-07-05T07:21:06Z","body":"@matheusmdx Oh dang, you're right! Doubled negations always throw me off 😅 \"On iOS, this method has **no** effect if ProjectSettings.display/window/handheld/orientation is **not** set to SCREEN_SENSOR.\"\nAny idea what the reasoning behind that restriction is? Does not seem intuitive to me. In our app we want everything but some screens to be portrait, and since there seems to be no way to get the current orientation of a device (screen_get_rotation only returns the setting, not the actual orientation) we use only one landscape direction to be able to size/position the safe area (notch) correctly.\nAnd more importantly it's inconcsistent with the behaviour on Android, where screen_set_orientation works also with non-sensor orientation settings.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4885222461/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4885731913","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118350#issuecomment-4885731913","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118350","id":4885731913,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABIzZaSQ","user":{"login":"matheusmdx","id":44306054,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzA2MDU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44306054?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx","html_url":"https://github.com/matheusmdx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.git